  "notes": "Measured on A6-EOE's two photos of 2025-04-02 at Sydney (left level, right from a little below). The gradient from purple to green is drawn as three bands; the fine diagonal lines in the panel, the white stars and the small Wimbledon logo by the forward door aren't drawn. The panel's lower edge is seen only on the right (the wing hides it on the left): just under the main deck's windows at the front, dipping toward the red sweep's tip. On the right the roundel and players measure lower between the decks than on the left (the right photo is from below and its heights are the less sure); the left's are used for both, lowered by 0.1 in y where the fitted window rows showed the fit reading high there (the lettering sits just under the upper deck's windows and on the main deck's). The roundel is a sponsor's mark (proposed as our own simplified mark, UAE/wimbledon-roundel); the two players are drawn figures, described with `licensed` and not proposed as marks (whose artwork they are isn't stated: credited here to Wimbledon, whose campaign they illustrate). Status: the newest open photo is 2025-04-02; a webcam sighting on 2026-11-03 (lead only) has it still in this scheme. Emirates' Grand Slam A380 (A6-EUH, January 2026) is a separate jet. Dated 2024-06 from the press release; A6-EOE is the jet in the photos and AirlineGeeks' story.",
  "history": "Unveiled for The Championships 2024 (June 2024), Emirates' first year as Wimbledon's official airline partner; the jet is in the 2023 scheme under the panel."
}
